{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fdf6ee1a91bff1edb92a7dfee727f8aed87a10deea1966f87187b0e060ce78fc","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI interface and bridge command subsystem","key_entities":["rebar bridge fsck","rebar bridge check-access","rebar bridge setup","bridge-fsck","bridge-probe","jira-onboard","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","docs/adr/0070-jira-onboard-config-write.md","scripts/canary_bridge.py","tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py","tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py"],"problem_keywords":["cli verb rename","command interface migration","backwards compatibility"],"propositions":["Three legacy CLI verbs (`rebar bridge-fsck`, `rebar bridge-probe`, `rebar jira-onboard`) must be renamed to noun-based spellings (`rebar bridge fsck`, `rebar bridge check-access`, `rebar bridge setup`) with the old spellings retained as functional compatibility entrypoints","All in-tree consumers including CLI dispatch arms, help text, configuration schemas, test assertions, scripts, workflows, and documentation must be migrated to canonical new spellings while preserving behavior parity","The new spellings must become the primary documented and generated reference form while old spellings continue to execute the identical implementation without forking behavior or state effects","Each rename requires string-level migration of hardcoded references in tests (`monkeypatch.setattr`, literal command strings), help files, schemas, and documentation beyond symbol-graph search","Compatibility enforcement necessitates repository-wide validation ensuring no uncategorized stale references to old spellings exist in live code while explicitly categorizing allowed uses (compatibility tests, migration notes, ADR history)","The implementation must preserve all existing functionality including option handling, exit codes, output schemas, and specific behaviors (e.g., `bridge setup` calls `bridge check-access` with env overlay, `--no-validate` flag skipping)"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787418039039426001,"uuid":"e53818ac-482e-483a-9477-4b0530275813"}